{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["And the reason of <b>and you shall return to YHWH your Elohim, and you shall obey His voice according to all that I command you this day, you and your children</b> (Deuteronomy 30:2), is that you shall return to YHWH with all your heart and with all your soul, and you shall accept upon yourself and upon your children for all their generations to do according to all that I command you this day — as they did in the second redemption, as it is written (Nehemiah 10:30): \"and entered into a curse and an oath, to walk in the Torah of Elohim which was given by the hand of Moses the servant of Elohim, and to observe and do all the commandments of YHWH our Master, and His ordinances and His statutes.\" Or <b>I command you, you and your children</b> may be like מְצַוְּךָ לְךָ וּלְבָנֶיךָ (I command you, to you and to your children), as in the expression וְאַתָּה צֻוֵּיתָ (Genesis 45:19), and likewise וַיָּרֵעוּ אוֹתָנוּ (Deuteronomy 26:6), meaning us. And in my opinion there is in it a great secret, for it alludes to what they said (Yevamot 63a): \"The Son of David will not come until all the souls in the body are exhausted,\" and I have already spoken of it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The Ramban references his earlier discussion of this Talmudic aggadah, which appears in his commentary on Genesis 2:7."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:56:54.841102331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}